## Frequently asked questions

{% faq-item question="Can I run OpenObserve and Uncoil together?" answer="Yes, and for teams with both real infrastructure breadth and real agent-specific needs, this is the most common stable setup: OpenObserve covers logs, metrics, and general traces across all services, while Uncoil covers agent-specific traces, cost, and evaluation for the LLM workload specifically." /%}

{% faq-item question="Does OpenObserve support LLM or agent tracing at all?" answer="It ingests OpenTelemetry spans from any source, including LLM calls, so basic trace storage and search work. It has no built-in concept of prompts, tool calls, evaluation, or provider cost, so those require custom instrumentation and dashboards on top of the generic span data." /%}

{% faq-item question="Is self-hosting OpenObserve actually cheaper than Uncoil?" answer="It depends on volume and what you're comparing. Infrastructure cost alone is often lower at scale, but total cost of ownership includes operator time and, if you want evaluation or cost tracking, the engineering time to build and maintain that layer yourself — which frequently outweighs the infrastructure savings at low-to-moderate agent volume." /%}

{% faq-item question="Why doesn't Uncoil do infrastructure monitoring?" answer="It's a deliberate scope choice, not a missing feature waiting to ship. Building agent-specific depth well — evaluation, cost attribution, session context — is a different product than building infrastructure breadth well, and trying to do both usually means doing neither at the level a dedicated tool can." /%}

{% faq-item question="What's the biggest hidden cost when self-hosting OpenObserve for LLM observability?" answer="Not the infrastructure bill — the ongoing engineering time to build and keep current an evaluation harness and a provider pricing table, both of which need maintenance every time a model changes, a provider adjusts pricing, or a new agent ships." /%}
